WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.000
DriveTTO searches over trajectories at test time. The planner stays frozen.

2
00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:18.000
Each candidate is a complete eight-pose trajectory. The current reference is always included.

3
00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:27.000
Archive the full trajectory's utility at its achieved endpoint, then guide the next request.

4
00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:36.000
Proposal and bounded-control branches refine the shared reference.

5
00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:45.000
Each scorer compares candidate and current reference in the same bank for this comparison.

6
00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:54.000
Smooth weights blend branch positions along the same future horizon; headings use circular interpolation.

7
00:00:54.000 --> 00:01:03.000
After admission checks, the minimum predicted gain drives selection; otherwise keep the current reference.

8
00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:12.000
This NAV1 Full schematic explains the mechanism. Benchmark schedules differ; parameters stay frozen.
